{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When one makes extraordinary.</b> This is among the forms that have two aspects in their interpretation: a root of separation and a root of building, for we find ״כי יפלא ממך דבר למשפט.״ And the pericah of the nazir is juxtaposed to the pericah of the sotah, to teach that most transgressions are caused by wine and a woman — she who does not properly groom the hair of her head does not seek intercourse." "<b>A nazirite vow, to abstain.</b> Corresponding to the three matters in the nazirite: wine, shaving, and impurity."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:40.091044010Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}